"""Scientific TASK for the agreed reusable A105 assay assessments.

These instructions explain source interpretation and numerical operand meaning.
They do not expose a worksheet schema or infer scientific facts from discovery.
"""
from .literature_assay_grading import ASSAY_TYPE_LABELS, COMMON_CRITERIA, CRITERIA_BY_TYPE, CRITERION_QUESTIONS


_TYPE_LABELS = ASSAY_TYPE_LABELS


ASSAY_GRADING_TASK = """Evaluate the selected assay using its reusable protocol type, measured quantity and functional assertion. Follow A105 experimental evidence subscore → subscoring grader → subscoring reader. Select the applicable existing protocol group below, then select readers for the needed measurements and their actual source format. Molecule identities, reagents, conditions and source locations are operands and applicability evidence; a paper or protein–substrate example is not a grader type. Preserve the exact functional resolution of rates, finite conversion, composition, reaction accounting, binding, transport, protein signal and amount.

Populate the same reusable template separately for each relevant actual experiment; this grading step is required, not an optional follow-up to source reading. Save an initial partial subscoring sheet using supported operands and explicit unknown or unavailable components, then refine the same experiment's assessment when further evidence is obtained. Missing controls, uncertainty, target correspondence or a fully available overall value do not justify leaving the experiment ungraded. Omit grading only when the examined material contains no applicable experiment or experimental result, retaining the source-bound reason. The grader saves its sheet independently of whether the parent's immediate return requests any cells. Preserve its source-anchored experiment_ref and the original physical measurement keys. A different experiment supplies another instance; a repeated representation or revised extraction remains tied to its original experiment and does not establish independent evidence. Retain complementary assays and disagreements. Saving or revising the grading sheet automatically updates dependent subscoring and main evidence scoring sheets before the original action's credit is observed. The existing scientific bindings and combination rules remain reliability SUM, validity SUM, relevance MAXIMUM, attribution MAXIMUM and overall SUM. Do not select another action merely to copy or refresh saved scores.

Establish the required records within the original reasoning action. Use its source_subjects to record an assay reference with reference_type assay, a literal label and an exact source anchor identifying the experiment. Record the proposed molecular function through hypotheses, preserving its actual functional resolution. An observation records what the source reports about that experiment; link it to the assay through source_subject_refs. An assessment records that source finding's relationship to the specified hypothesis through observation_ref and hypothesis_ref. Choose the applicable purpose-specific grader from the supplied table. Each evidence_processing.gradings entry contains arguments: the JSON encoding of that selected grader's argument object. Its experiment_ref identifies the actual assay and its assertion_ref identifies the proposed function. Use @aliases for records established in this same action and existing IDs for records already saved; do not recreate an unchanged experiment or hypothesis. The host saves the source records and selected grader's partial sheet together. For interpretations.support_refs and prediction_model.support_refs, select possessed source_subjects records (record_type reference) carrying an original anchor with source_ref, artifact_ref, start, end and quote. Select their same-action @aliases or already saved reference IDs. These anchored records identify the passages supporting the custom criteria. Preserve unknown interpretations when support is missing and use an empty support_refs list when no supporting passage is established. Copy a supplied argument reference directly when invoking a subsequent operation.

To create a text anchor, select its received source_ref, artifact_ref and zero-based half-open UTF-8 start/end. A text witness instead selects source_ref, representation and start/end. The host retrieves and stores the exact quotation from those selected bytes within the original action, before validating and grading the records. You choose the passage and its scientific meaning; no quote transcription or separate quotation action is required. Stored supporting references retain the complete authenticated anchor.

Every evidence assessment must include investigation_finding with its actual source_claim, qualification and retained/withdrawn status using the common schema. State what the source establishes about the actual assayed molecule and experiment, retaining unknown or different source-to-target relationships. The iterator and parent consume that recorded scientific finding; the saved numerical sheet alone does not supply it. Do not manufacture an input-molecule claim or target correspondence to obtain credit. Preparatory entities, contexts and candidate hypotheses remain metadata rather than evidence assessments.

All groups feed the same reliability, validity, relevance and attribution dimensions. Keep comparability outside the intended experimental change explicit. For the selected estimate, examine these common questions: """ + " ".join(
    name + ': ' + CRITERION_QUESTIONS[name] for name in COMMON_CRITERIA
) + "\n\n" + "\n\n".join(
    label + ' (' + kind + '): ' + ' '.join(
        name + ': ' + CRITERION_QUESTIONS[name] for name in CRITERIA_BY_TYPE[kind] if name not in COMMON_CRITERIA)
    for kind, label in _TYPE_LABELS.items()
) + """

The interpretation keys for a selected assay_type are exactly the common keys above plus that protocol group's keys. Omit keys belonging to other groups; unknown means an unresolved criterion within the selected group. Apply only the questions relevant to the selected quantity and assertion. A descriptive rate comparison need not fit a kinetic model. A substrate-disappearance or completion-time result does not itself claim an identified product; an amount or time result need not be a conversion fraction. A finite composition need not be equilibrium. Where the contract permits not_applicable, support that interpretation from the actual question and source. Otherwise preserve supported, unknown and conflicting interpretations distinctly, with the applicable source witnesses. A control's label alone does not establish its adequacy, and a reported count alone does not establish independent preparations.

Reuse activity_rate for enzyme kinetics, substrate-specificity comparisons, optical rates and rate-based partner omission/addback. Choose the actual kinetic parameter or contrast quantity without interpreting higher Km as higher activity. An optical NADH-depletion rate remains its measured reporter endpoint unless the coupling and attribution evidence establishes the claimed reaction. For omission/addback contrasts use the partner quantity and examine the perturbation criteria; the partner's intended change is not a nuisance-condition penalty.

Use ligand_binding for binding parameters and discrimination, retaining IC50 versus Kd, fit/model meaning, ligand mapping and nonspecific controls. Use transport_response for the actual uptake, saturation, electrical or ion-discrimination quantity; a saturation correction is not an independently measured flux, and charge equivalents do not identify the transported ion. Use protein_signal for reported ratios or gel display measurements, preserving loading, exposure, ROI and detector limits; display darkness is not calibrated molecular occupancy. Use protein_amount for amount, preparation-composition and active-site measurements; mass fraction is not active fraction or contaminating activity. These supporting measurements can inform the same A105 assessment without becoming direct functional evidence by relabeling.

Select the grader by the experiment's protocol and question, not the reader's format. A controlled gel-shift binding experiment may use ligand_binding with its native band_display_fraction and binding-specific controls; it need not claim a fitted Kd or calibrated occupancy. A kinetic reader's actual Km may populate transport_response as transport_parameter when it belongs to the studied transport system and fit. Preserve that preparation and concentration scope rather than treating a shared reader as a fixed assay assignment.

Select effect as the already reported or calculated native quantity being assessed. When source.experimental.records supplies a database_measurement selector, use that selector directly as quantities.effect; the grader reads the retained value, unit and physical measurement identity. Native database JSON does not need to be reread as a literature table or converted through a kinetic reader first. For each other operand not established by the source, use null. Use unknown for an unresolved criterion and retain its actual support_refs; missing support uses an empty support_refs list. These are supported partial inputs, not a request to acquire more data before grading. Do not mark an unresolved criterion not_applicable merely because its evidence is missing.

The source_number shortcut accepts a number immediately followed by its printed unit. For a single reported Km, kcat or catalytic-efficiency value in a table without a native database selector, with its unit in a separate table header, use literature.kinetic.populate with separate exact number and unit witnesses, the parameter as numerator, and no denominator. Request numerator_parameter and pass the returned literature_kinetic_cells sheet/component into this grader as a received_component. The unit witness selects the complete unit token, including its exponent markup when present; parameter labels and neighboring values have their own witnesses. This applies to paper and database tables alike. After a reader rejects a layout, select the implemented reader for that representation; a layout rejection does not establish that the source measurement is absent. If the available readers cannot represent the quantity, retain that specific unsupported-reader limitation separately from missing source data.

Select effect_variance only as the variance of that exact estimate on its squared unit scale, retaining its corrections and shared inputs. Select recovery as an applicable measured recovery ratio; attributed_signal and total_signal as the supported same-endpoint contribution and denominator; and condition_test and condition_reference as a nuisance-condition comparison outside the intended experimental change. Keep the intended test/reference change out of that nuisance correction. These operands support separate diagnostics; do not multiply them into an effect that already includes their corrections or turn them into universal quality weights.

Select assertion_prediction and alternative_prediction only from explicit predictions for the same quantity, units, assertion and experimental conditions. Neither the observed effect nor a desirable result supplies an independent prediction. An overall experimental-evidence score is required. Select the applicable supported comparison model: known-variance normal, an explicitly justified normal approximation using estimated variance, or a Student-t residual model using estimated variance and source-supported degrees of freedom. A reported SD is not automatically the variance of the selected estimate, and estimated variance does not become known variance. Student-t degrees of freedom must belong to that estimator; a displayed sample count alone does not supply them. If the appropriate model, predictions, exact estimate variance or scientific support is unavailable, report the score as unresolved with its actual missing-input or unsupported-model reason while returning useful native measurements and supported diagnostics. Do not describe that limitation as an optional scoring requirement. The signed log evidence ratio is not a function probability, target-transfer weight or final annotation credit.

Preserve below-detection or other censored observations together with their actual limits, units and assay context. An observed upper or lower limit can enter the selected comparison through its event probability; it must not become zero or an observed threshold value. A confidence interval, error bar, graph-reading interval or range over ambiguous readings is not a censored observation. If no numerical limit or applicable reporting model is established, retain that specific unresolved limitation.

Use received numerical components, authenticated literal source spans, or the supplied database_measurement effect reader as the operation permits; do not enter model-authored measurements. Database selectors identify actual retained rows and fields; the reader retrieves values, units, relations and measurement identity. PubChem result definitions and MaveDB score metadata must belong to the selected assay. For multiplexed binding experiments, relative_binding_response and log_relative_binding_response preserve the source's reported response scale; establish its definition and reference construct from the assay before selecting either. A native_score unit preserves the deposited scale and does not imply affinity or a shared scale across studies. Reuse the original experiment reference when the paper and a database represent the same experiment. Preserve graph-reading uncertainty separately from experimental variation, shared observations across assays, complementary endpoints and contradictions. Return exactly the requested saved A105 components and necessary scientific qualifications through the parent's typed form. Distinguish unselected information, missing source evidence and unsupported readers/calculations/bindings. An extracted number alone does not complete the assay assessment, and unavailable fields are not zero scores."""

ASSAY_GRADING_OPERATION_DESCRIPTION = (
    'Populate the same A105 experimental evidence dimensions using one selected reusable assay type: '
    'activity/rate (including kinetics, optical rates and partner perturbations), endpoint conversion, '
    'product distribution, reaction coupling, binding, transport, protein signal or protein amount. '
    'Retain each actual experiment as its own instance of the same reusable template, with '
    'experiment identity and shared physical measurements preserved. '
    'Select scientific applicability by protocol, quantity and design, then select possessed reader '
    'components or authenticated source numbers by their actual capability and source format. '
    'source_number requires an adjacent printed unit. A reported kinetic parameter with a shared '
    'table-header unit can use literature.kinetic.populate and its received numerator_parameter component. '
    'Return requested native effect, reliability, validity, attribution, comparability and '
    'assertion-comparison components with source-supported interpretations. The overall log evidence '
    'ratio requires explicit fixed predictions and a supported known-normal, estimated-normal approximation '
    'or Student-t residual model. Preserve estimated uncertainty, actual degrees of freedom and observed '
    'censoring limits; do not treat reading ranges as censoring. Scores remain conditional, and missing '
    'inputs preserve partials. Existing corrections are not applied twice. '
    'No case-specific grader, general parser capability, target transfer or annotation credit is inferred.'
)

__all__ = ['ASSAY_GRADING_TASK', 'ASSAY_GRADING_OPERATION_DESCRIPTION']
